# state/eval-log/*.jsonl -- jonhill90/skills#230's own append-only,
# one-file-per-skill eval observation log (agent-b3.md's fix for
# state/eval-status.json generating a merge conflict per PR, three times
# in one night: #239, #240, #243).
#
# merge=union (git's own built-in driver) is load-bearing, not decoration
# -- verified by driving a real git merge, not assumed: two branches
# BOTH appending a new observation to the SAME skill's log file, off a
# shared base, conflict under git's DEFAULT text merge even though both
# sides only ever add a line at the end of the file (git's 3-way line
# merge treats two inserts anchored at the same trailing context as
# overlapping). union resolves it automatically, keeping BOTH
# observations in the order their own commits reached the merge -- the
# exact "two independent evaluations of the same skill must both survive"
# requirement this fix exists to satisfy, checked with
# tests/test_eval_status.py's own TestConflictDemonstration, not asserted.
state/eval-log/*.jsonl merge=union
